{"_meta":{"securitySchemes":[{"scopes":["odds.read"],"type":"oauth2"}]},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Today's board (live odds)"},"description":"The app Live board (GET live/board): upcoming and in-play games with their main-market prices, optional league or sport, limit 1-20 and cursor. sport reads a sport chip's board across its leagues (SPRT_tennis, SPRT_soccer, SPRT_golf; tennis and golf games have no league). A league outside the app's chips is built on its first read, so that first answer can be 503 provider_unavailable with retryAfterSeconds: read again in about 60 s. Only leagues in season with a DraftKings price right now are listed: a league or sport without one answers no games (it is not in get_league_order either) and comes back by itself once its games are priced. mode: live with includeStatus: true lists only the games in play now, each with its status (a game in a league with no scoreboard feed, such as tennis or UFC, is listed while DraftKings prices it in play: its status is in_progress with the score, period and clock a public scoreboard has for it, or none; tennis: score = sets won, period = the set in play, displayClock = that set's games home-away; UFC: period = round); with includeStatus: true, eventSeries gives each game its playoff series line (round, game, summary; MLB now) or null; stale: true means some games could not be confirmed yet, so read again shortly. Use category: event_catalog for original event market identities, event_prices for an exact source-bound group at one book, or board_snapshot for one prewarmed page; those require request. Decision support; never a wager.","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"category":{"description":"Source-bound categories require request; board_snapshot reads one complete prewarmed page without provider work; games uses the board filters.","enum":["games","event_catalog","event_prices","board_sna